-- on its own --
<2 bytes>
<0 bytes>
<10 bytes>
-- interpolated, which is the same rendering --
<2 bytes> and <0 bytes>
-- as a field, where a String next to it is quoted and it is not --
Blob { name: "a\nb", data: <2 bytes> }
-- as a constructor payload --
One(<10 bytes>)
Empty
-- through a dictionary: an Option payload and a list element --
Some(<2 bytes>)
None
[<2 bytes>, <0 bytes>]
-- and in a tuple, whose witness is built from its elements --
(<2 bytes>, 1)
(<2 bytes>, "s", <10 bytes>)
-- the summary is the length, so a concatenation shows the sum --
<12 bytes>
12
<3 bytes>
